{:pi "0.63.1", :refs "src/domain/stellar.clj src/domain/phase0.clj test/domain/stellar_test.clj", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Fixed star ignition bug: fusion never fired in parallel pipeline due to one-tick buffer lag (classifier read stale density from frozen snapshot), and luminosity was always 0 because fusion-system skipped :star bodies. Added fusion-promotion-system barrier that runs after the fold to check fusion-possible? with post-contraction density/pressure. Star now ignites at main-sequence with L=1e29. Added regression test. 195 tests pass.", :ts "2026-06-28T02:33:48.614Z", :host "local", :kind :decision, :origin "pi", :repo "/home/err/spaces/Truth", :owner "receipt-river"}
{:pi "0.63.1", :refs "src/domain/stellar.clj test/domain/stellar_test.clj", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Fixed disappearing-star bug. Root cause: stellar-merge-handler volume-summed radii (r'=cbrt(rl^3+rs^3)). A compact star (R~1e8 m) accreting a freshly-condensed diffuse body (R~1e11-1e13 m, a fluid smoothing radius) ballooned to cloud size. temperature-system derives T=virial(M,R)~1/R every tick for stars, collapsing the bloated star to ~1e3 K, and structure-system never re-contracts a :star -> star became a cold diffuse blob still tagged :star ('disappeared'). High-dv merges spiked impact heating to billions K for one tick before virial crashed it. Fix: conserve survivor density on accretion (r'=rl*cbrt(total/ml)) instead of volume-summing. Verified headless: star stays T~2.2e7 K, R~6.5e8 m, max-T-ever 2.8e7 (no billions), stable 4000 ticks. Collision/accretion uses accretion-radius (feeding zone), not body radius, so compacting body radius is safe. 196 tests pass.", :ts "2026-06-28T03:34:33.000Z", :host "local", :kind :decision, :origin "pi", :repo "/home/err/spaces/Truth", :owner "receipt-river"}
{:pi "0.63.1", :refs "src/domain/physics/collision.clj src/domain/stellar.clj src/domain/phase0.clj test/domain/phase0_test.clj", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Redesigned Phase 0 growth into the sink-particle split and deleted the legacy sequential runtime. (1) collidable-bodies now uses physical radius, not the 50x feeding zone -> resolved bodies merge only on literal collision (fixes bodies poofing together while far apart). (2) sink-formation-system generalized from newly-formed debris/protostars to ALL sinks incl stars -> bodies grow by accreting gas. (3) Deleted sequential pipeline: physics-systems fn, :phase0/parallel? flag, step-physics branch, dead thermal-system fn, and the sequential test-full-simulation; step-physics is parallel-only (one runtime, no-two-sims rule). Headless verify (gas-count 400, adaptive): stars stay compact+hot, no disappearance, gas accretes (nebula 310->57), forms a stable ~5-star cluster (0.4 Msun, T~1.8e7). Trade-off: cluster not one dominant star. Orphaned legacy fns collapse/classify/jeans-collapse-system kept by unit tests only. 195 tests, 0 failures.", :ts "2026-06-28T04:05:08.000Z", :host "local", :kind :decision, :origin "pi", :repo "/home/err/spaces/Truth", :owner "receipt-river"}
{:pi "0.63.1", :refs "src/domain/stellar.clj src/domain/phase0.clj src/domain/ecs/components.clj test/domain/stellar_test.clj docs/specs/phase0-stellar-winds-and-mass-loss.md", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Implemented phase A of stellar winds / mass loss (spec: phase0-stellar-winds-and-mass-loss.md). stellar-wind-system (serial barrier after sink-formation): stars shed mass at Mdot=k*L/(v_esc*c), banked in new c/wind-reservoir; when it reaches one wind-parcel mass a :nebula parcel is launched radially (momentum-conserving recoil), reabsorbed by sink-formation -> competitive accretion as visible gas flow. Load-bearing invariant: a collapsed body NEVER returns to :nebula; mass-loss demotes star->brown-dwarf->debris (classify-next-state down-ladder), only shed material becomes gas. Fixed a mass-leak bug (parcel must materialize from reservoir, not re-debit star mass). Verified: total mass (bodies+reservoir) conserved to 7e-16; dominant star grew 0.29->0.74 Msun via reabsorption; demotion never yields :nebula. Cinematic default :phase0/wind-rate-scale 5.0. 197 tests, 0 failures.", :ts "2026-06-28T04:34:27.000Z", :host "local", :kind :decision, :origin "pi", :repo "/home/err/spaces/Truth", :owner "receipt-river"}
{:pi "0.63.1", :refs "src/domain/stellar.clj docs/specs/phase0-stellar-winds-and-mass-loss.md", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Fixed wind blow-up: parcels launched at physical v_esc (~5.6e5 m/s) over Myr-scale dt traveled ~3 nebula radii/tick, flinging the whole system apart (extent 1.6e16->4e18 m, speeds->5.6e5 in 80 ticks; 'chaotic, stars flung everywhere, no gas'). Root: realistic wind speed incompatible with the timestep. Fix: cap wind drift to v-fac (default 0.15) of the feeding zone per tick — model the observable shed envelope, not the km/s wind. After cap: speeds stay ~120 m/s, extent steady 1.6e16, gas stays visible, mass conserved exactly, demotion to brown-dwarf intact. 197 tests, 0 failures.", :ts "2026-06-28T04:41:35.000Z", :host "local", :kind :decision, :origin "pi", :repo "/home/err/spaces/Truth", :owner "receipt-river"}
{:pi "0.63.1", :refs "src/domain/stellar.clj src/domain/phase0.clj test/domain/stellar_test.clj docs/specs/phase0-stellar-winds-and-mass-loss.md", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Implemented winds spec phase B: stellar-flare-system (barrier after stellar-wind). Episodic CMEs — every flare-period ticks per star (default 30), bigger (flare-mass-factor x wind-parcel, default 3) and hotter (flare-temp-factor x virial, default 3) blobs ejected BIPOLAR along the spin axis, mass debited from the star (conserved), drift velocity-capped (flare-speed-factor default 0.4) like the wind so no blow-up. Guard: never flares a star below half the H-burning mass. Verified: stable (speeds ~120 m/s, extent steady), mass conserved exactly, flares fire (6 hot bursts/80 ticks, peak nebula T 1.8e7 K). Fresh flares reabsorbed within ~2 ticks by the feeding zone (bright flicker, not durable CME — tuning/phase C later). Regression test added. 198 tests, 0 failures. Phase C (Roche/tidal stripping) still pending.", :ts "2026-06-28T04:49:07.000Z", :host "local", :kind :decision, :origin "pi", :repo "/home/err/spaces/Truth", :owner "receipt-river"}
{:pi "0.63.1", :refs "src/domain/em.clj", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Fixed magnetic flux-freezing annihilation (root cause of no visible field lines). field-system computes B=flux/R^2 with flux decayed by resistive-decay using rate=eta/r^2, eta=1e8. For a contracted core (r~3e8) the decay timescale r^2/eta ~ 1e9 s is far below the Myr-scale dt (~1e11 s), so flux lost exp(-100)~everything PER TICK -> a forming star's B collapsed to ~5.6e-71 T instead of amplifying. Same large-dt coupling hazard as the stellar wind. Fix: lower eta default 1e8->1e4 (gentle physical decay) and floor the per-tick retention factor at min-flux-retention=0.97 (dt-robust cap). Verified: a star now forms with B amplified 1e-9->1.4e-2 T (was 5.6e-71); field-line brightness saturates so lines are visible on protostars/stars. 198 tests, 0 failures.", :ts "2026-06-28T05:13:51.000Z", :host "local", :kind :decision, :origin "pi", :repo "/home/err/spaces/Truth", :owner "receipt-river"}
{:pi "0.63.1", :refs "src/domain/em.clj src/infra/render.clj src/infra/dev/server.clj", :dod "receipt-river", :manifest "none", :note "Modeled magnetism as a FIELD (not per-body sticks): added dipole-moment, dipole-field-at, net-field-at, external-field-at, field-sources to domain.em. Each body is a magnetic dipole; the field at any point is the superposition, defined everywhere; star-star/planet-star interaction emerges and is range-dependent (1/r^3) - verified: 2 stars 2 radii apart feel ~8.75e-4 T of each other (6% of intrinsic), negligible by 1e12 m. Honest simulation finding: dipole coupling matters only for very close pairs (binaries, moons), not distant stars. Added render/field-line-shapes (dipole loops per body, oriented on moment, sized to drawn radius) + phase0-bodies+fields wired as the dev bodies-fn. STATUS: physics verified; flux-freezing fix verified live (B 1e-9->~5e-3 T); field-line VISUAL generates correct geometry (1056 segs) but loops not yet reading well on screen (camera-zoom scale mismatch) - needs tuning. 198 tests, 0 failures.", :ts "2026-06-28T05:53:41.000Z", :host "local", :kind :decision, :origin "pi", :repo "/home/err/spaces/Truth", :owner "receipt-river"}
