{:refs "docs/specs/seed-and-grow-condensation-realspec.md docs/designs/resolution-regimes-and-scale-coupling.md 0d03d0f", :manifest "none", :note "DECISIONS for handoff: (1) The ~669 M-earth (2.1 M_J) body floor = one gas parcel (nebula-mass/gas-count = 4e30/1000 = 4e27 kg). It is a START VALUE + the 'body=whole parcel' promotion rule, NOT a physics law and NOT a Lagrangian necessity (Lagrangian only floors GAS resolution). (2) Fix = SEED-AND-GROW: condensation spawns a small physical seed (~1e15-1e18 kg from condensation physics), debits parent parcel, grows via M3 gradual BHL (grow half already built, 0.58ms). Decouples body mass from parcel mass; gets Chicxulub/Moon/Earth-scale bodies. Spec written. (3) Sub-astronomical scales (crust voxels 1e12 kg, life 1e0 kg) need NESTED per-planet mass budgets (LOD content layers coupled by M5 handoff) — forced by float precision: a 4e27 parcel's ULP is ~1e12 kg, so finer masses cannot be bookkept as parcel debits. Design note written. (4) Do NOT bump gas-count: bench shows super-linear (1000=32ms/30fps, 2000=64ms, 4000=139ms, 8000=332ms/3fps) — grain is compute-locked for real-time. (5) M3 mass-transfer benchmarked at 0.58ms = 2% of tick (1 sink) — EXONERATED as the 17.6->~30ms tick drift; drift source is elsewhere, profile it. Artifacts: docs/specs/seed-and-grow-condensation-realspec.md, docs/designs/resolution-regimes-and-scale-coupling.md, kanban cards seed-and-grow-condensation / mass-transfer-benchmark / tick-perf-drift-profile.", :ts "2026-07-06T23:49:35.556017542Z", :host "local", :kind :decision, :origin "body-mass floor / multi-scale resolution design (handoff to kimi)", :owner "receipt-river"}
